  "description": "Approval digests (STANDARD v1.2.0 sections 5.14 and 5.18.7, normative under section 10.3), computed by the reference executor (core/src/exec/machine.rs, core/src/exec/canonical.rs). Each `step` vector is one approval request of a workflow step; each `tool_call` vector is the approval of a tool call. The shown values are a JSON array; the digest is the SHA-256 of the UTF-8 encoding of their canonical JSON (RFC 8785), as 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits, compared regardless of case. An implementation that computes or checks approval digests produces each vector's `canonical` text and `digest` from its `shown` values; an executor shows each `step` vector's `shown` values, given its `inputs` or `bindings` and any `recheck_read`, and a safety layer each `tool_call` vector's. This file is printable ASCII: any other character is written as a JSON \\u escape, so no tool that normalises or transcodes text can change a vector.",
